From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:16:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/30] Preserve native TLS through an opt-in fixed-destination
 gateway

tls_passthrough relays to the name in the SNI. Some workers need the
origin certificate end to end with a single destination the actor cannot
change.

--native-tls-destination=HOST:PORT serves only that destination. Each
CONNECT requires an actor identity UID that matches the running actor, a
current policy with exactly one tls_passthrough rule for that host and
port, and no policy cache. The listener relays to a static cluster, so the
CONNECT address never picks the upstream.

TestNativeTLSEnvoy runs the real Envoy image and dynamic module through
hack/test-native-tls.sh, and a pr-workflow job runs it.

Fork-Topic: native-tls-gateway
Fork-Upstream: fork-only
